# Copy to .env (NOT .env.local) and fill in once real values exist.
#
# THIS FILE IS FOR THE PRISMA CLI ONLY - `prisma migrate`, `prisma validate`,
# `prisma studio`, run by hand from this directory. It has nothing to do with
# the deployed Worker, which never reads a .env file: that reads .dev.vars
# locally (see .dev.vars.example) and `wrangler secret put <NAME>` in
# production. Two separate files for two separate tools that happen to want
# the same string is the Prisma CLI's own convention (it reads .env and
# nothing else, unconditionally - see fragrance-dupes/.env.example, which
# said this before prisma/schema.prisma moved here on 2026-09-16), not
# something invented for this project.
#
# Confirmed by running `prisma validate` in this directory with no .env
# present: it fails with "Environment variable not found: DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED"
# rather than silently succeeding, which is what prompted writing this file
# down instead of leaving it undocumented.

# Postgres. See prisma/schema.prisma's datasource block and neon.ts for why
# there are two strings, and MARKETPLACE-PLAN.md §4 / PRODUCER-PROGRAM.md §8
# (fragrance-dupes/, where the surrounding plan was written) for the wider
# context.
#
# DO NOT FILL THESE IN BY HAND. Run, from this directory:
#   neon link --project-id holy-sunset-91521586 --branch production -y
# It writes both into .env and refreshes them on later runs, so they cannot
# drift from the project. Requires `neon login` first.
#
# POOLED (hostname contains '-pooler'): not used by the Prisma CLI directly,
# but kept here too so this file is a complete, self-consistent copy of what
# `neon link` produces - and because the Worker's own DATABASE_URL secret
# (.dev.vars.example) is copied from this same value.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
# DIRECT (same host WITHOUT '-pooler'): what `prisma migrate` actually reads
# (schema.prisma's `directUrl`). Using the pooled URL here makes migrations
# hang or fail without naming the real cause - `prisma validate` failing on
# this exact line, with no .env present, is what confirmed this file was
# needed rather than assumed.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# NEVER COMMIT THE REAL VALUES. This repo is public. .env* is gitignored at
# the repo root (with !.env.example carved out) - verify with
# `git check-ignore .env` before assuming it. Anyone who reads a leaked
# string has full read/write on the producer database; rotate in the Neon
# dashboard if one ever escapes.
